  "verbalization": "Pemirolast is implicated in the pathogenesis of Intrinsic Asthma through a multi-step mechanism involving the induction of asthmatic responses. The evidence suggests that Pemirolast may act as a mediator in the progression of allergic asthma, leading to the activation of pathways that result in the development of Intrinsic Asthma. This is supported by the observed indication of Pemirolast in Allergic Asthma and its subsequent interaction with Ibudilast, which in turn is linked to Intrinsic Asthma. The presence of a direct indication from Pemirolast to Intrinsic Asthma, along with the indirect pathway through Ibudilast, indicates a potential role in the pathophysiology of the condition. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Pemirolast in the development of Intrinsic Asthma, particularly in the context of allergic asthma, where it may influence the inflammatory response and airway remodeling. The mechanism is supported by the observed clinical and pharmacological relationships, though further studies are needed to confirm the exact role of Pemirolast in the progression of Intrinsic Asthma.",
